<body>

<header>
    <div class="container">

        <div class="brand">
            <div class="brand-icon">🔒</div>
            Message Vault
        </div>

        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

        <p class="updated">
            Last updated: September 12, 2026
        </p>

    </div>
</header>

<main>

    <div class="container">

        <!-- Introduction -->
        <section>

            <span class="privacy-badge">
                Local-First &amp; Privacy Focused
            </span>

            <h2>1. Introduction</h2>

            <p>
                This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Message Vault</strong>
                ("the App", "we", "us", or "our") handles information when
                you use our Android application.
            </p>

            <p>
                Message Vault is designed as a local notification history
                application. The App can capture information that is displayed
                through Android notifications and store that information on
                your device.
            </p>

            <div class="highlight">
                <strong>Our core privacy principle:</strong>
                Message Vault is designed so that captured notification data
                remains on your device. We do not operate a server that receives
                or stores your message content.
            </div>

        </section>

        <!-- Information collected -->
        <section>

            <h2>2. Information We Process</h2>

            <p>
                Depending on your Android notification settings and the
                notifications generated by other applications, Message Vault
                may process information contained in notifications.
            </p>

            <p>This may include:</p>

            <ul>
                <li>Notification text.</li>
                <li>Sender or notification title.</li>
                <li>Application name or package name.</li>
                <li>Date and time of the notification.</li>
                <li>Notification metadata provided by Android.</li>
                <li>Other notification information made available through the Android notification system.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                The exact information available to the App depends on the
                notification generated by the source application and the
                Android version and settings on your device.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Notification access -->
        <section>

            <h2>3. Notification Access Permission</h2>

            <p>
                Message Vault uses Android's
                <strong>Notification Listener Service</strong> to receive
                notifications that Android makes available to the App.
            </p>

            <p>
                This permission is required for the App's primary functionality.
                Without notification access, Message Vault cannot capture
                notification information.
            </p>

            <p>
                Notification Access may allow the App to receive notification
                content from applications whose notifications are visible to
                Android.
            </p>

            <p>
                You can revoke Notification Access at any time through your
                Android system settings.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Local storage -->
        <section>

            <h2>4. Local Storage</h2>

            <p>
                Captured notification information is intended to be stored
                locally on your Android device using the App's private storage.
            </p>

            <p>
                The App does not require an online account to store notification
                history.
            </p>

            <p>
                The App's core notification history functionality does not
                require uploading your message content to our servers.
            </p>

            <div class="highlight">
                <strong>Local-only design:</strong>
                Your captured notification history is intended to remain
                within the App's local storage unless you explicitly use a
                future feature that transfers or exports data.
            </div>

        </section>

        <!-- No cloud -->
        <section>

            <h2>5. No Cloud Storage of Message Content</h2>

            <p>
                Message Vault does not provide a cloud database for storing
                your captured notification content.
            </p>

            <p>
                We do not intentionally collect or upload your captured
                message content to our servers.
            </p>

            <p>
                The App should therefore be considered a
                <strong>local-first application</strong>.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Deleted messages -->
        <section>

            <h2>6. Deleted Messages and Notification History</h2>

            <p>
                Message Vault does not access, decrypt, or retrieve private
                databases belonging to other applications.
            </p>

            <p>
                The App works by storing information that was previously
                available through Android notifications.
            </p>

            <p>
                For example, if a notification contains a message and Message
                Vault captures that notification, a local copy of the
                notification information may remain in Message Vault even if
                the original message is subsequently deleted from the source
                application.
            </p>

            <div class="highlight">
                Message Vault cannot recover message content that was never
                available through an Android notification or that Android did
                not provide to the App.
            </div>

        </section>

        <!-- Third party apps -->
        <section>

            <h2>7. Third-Party Applications</h2>

            <p>
                Message Vault may process notifications generated by
                third-party applications installed on your device.
            </p>

            <p>
                Message Vault is independent from those third-party
                applications unless explicitly stated otherwise.
            </p>

            <p>
                We do not control how third-party applications generate,
                modify, or display their notifications.
            </p>

            <p>
                Their own privacy policies and terms may apply to their
                services.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Data sharing -->
        <section>

            <h2>8. Data Sharing</h2>

            <p>
                We do not sell, rent, or intentionally share your captured
                notification content with third parties.
            </p>

            <p>
                Because the App is designed around local storage, we do not
                need to receive your message content on a remote server for
                the core functionality to operate.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Analytics -->
        <section>

            <h2>9. Analytics and Diagnostics</h2>

            <p>
                The production version of the App should not send notification
                content, message content, sender names, or other private
                notification information to analytics or crash-reporting
                services.
            </p>

            <p>
                If analytics or diagnostic services are introduced in a future
                version, this Privacy Policy will be updated as necessary to
                explain what information is collected and why.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Security -->
        <section>

            <h2>10. Data Security</h2>

            <p>
                We take reasonable measures to protect information stored by
                the App.
            </p>

            <p>
                The App is designed to use Android's application-private
                storage and does not intentionally expose captured messages
                to other applications.
            </p>

            <p>
                However, no storage mechanism can be guaranteed to be
                completely secure. The security of your device, operating
                system, screen lock, and other device-level protections also
                affects the security of locally stored information.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Data retention -->
        <section>

            <h2>11. Data Retention</h2>

            <p>
                Captured notification history may remain on your device until
                it is deleted according to your selected retention settings or
                manually deleted by you.
            </p>

            <p>
                Depending on the App version, retention options may include
                automatic deletion after a defined period such as 7, 30, or
                90 days.
            </p>

            <p>
                You can also delete stored notification history through the
                App's data management settings.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Data deletion -->
        <section>

            <h2>12. Data Deletion</h2>

            <p>
                You can delete individual notification records or clear your
                notification history using the functionality provided by the
                App.
            </p>

            <p>
                You may also uninstall the App. Depending on Android's
                behavior and your device backup configuration, application
                data may be removed or handled according to Android's system
                policies.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Children's privacy -->
        <section>

            <h2>13. Children's Privacy</h2>

            <p>
                Message Vault is not specifically directed at children.
            </p>

            <p>
                We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
                through remote servers because the core application is
                designed to operate locally on the device.
            </p>

            <p>
                Parents or guardians should supervise device permissions and
                application usage where appropriate.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- User responsibility -->
        <section>

            <h2>14. User Responsibility</h2>

            <p>
                Because Message Vault can process notification content, users
                should carefully consider which applications are allowed to
                be monitored.
            </p>

            <p>
                You are responsible for using the App in accordance with
                applicable laws, regulations, third-party application terms,
                and the privacy expectations of other people whose messages
                may appear in your notifications.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Changes -->
        <section>

            <h2>15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
                changes to the App, applicable laws, or our privacy practices.
            </p>

            <p>
                When changes are made, the "Last updated" date at the top of
                this page will be updated.
            </p>

        </section>

        <!-- Contact -->
        <section>

            <h2>16. Contact Us</h2>

            <p>
                If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this
                Privacy Policy or the privacy practices of Message Vault,
                please contact us:
            </p>

            <p>
                <strong>Developer:</strong> Developer Name<br>
                <strong>Email:</strong>
                <a href="mailto:support@example.com">
                    support@example.com
                </a>
            </p>

        </section>

    </div>

</main>

<footer>
    <div class="container">
        &copy; 2026 Developer Name. All rights reserved.
    </div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
